course: dictionary
lesson: 8053
title: Gentle words, hard truths
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are chosen to sound gentler than what they mean. This is called a euphemism. «Rehomed» is one. A pet that is rehomed was given away to new owners because the old owners could not or would not keep it. Read the words around it to check what happened.
explain: Look at this sentence: «Our cat was rehomed last week, because we moved to a flat with no garden.» The cat did not disappear by magic. It went to new owners, and the reason was the move. The word tells you what happened, and the rest of the sentence tells you why.
explain: Use the swap check. Put "given away to new owners" in place of rehomed. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning. Rehomed can also describe a person or thing moved to a new home: «After the flood, the family was rehomed in a school hall.»
fact: Rehome means to find a new home for something, and a rehomed pet has been given away to new owners.
fact: «Rehomed» is the past form of the verb rehome (rehome, rehomes, rehomed, rehoming), and it can also be an adjective, as in a rehomed dog.
fact: A euphemism is a gentle word used in place of a harder one.
fact: Pet owners, shelters and parents use rehomed in every region, especially in the UK.
fact: Sometimes grown-ups say rehomed to hide that a pet died or was put down, so if you are not sure what happened, ask a grown-up kindly and plainly.
exercise: «The family was rehomed in a school hall after the flood.» What does rehomed mean here? | Painted a new colour | Given away as a pet | Cleaned from top to bottom | *Moved to a new home
exercise: «Our rabbit was rehomed when we moved house.» What does rehomed mean? | Locked in a shed | Born in the house | *Given away to new owners | Lost in the garden
exercise: Why might a grown-up say rehomed instead of a harder word? | To mean the pet was born there | Because it is a very long word | To show the pet is a dog | *To make a hard or sad thing sound gentler
test: «The shelter rehomed three kittens last Saturday.» What does rehomed mean? | Sold to a shop | *Given away to new owners | Locked in a cupboard | Left out in the rain
test: Which phrase is a good swap for rehomed in «Our dog was rehomed»? | Sat by the fire | Went out for a walk | *Given away to new owners | Chased a ball
exam: Why is rehomed called a euphemism? | It only ever means a dog | It is a Scottish word | *It sounds gentler than what really happened | It is always a long word
